<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Battuta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1334–1341 at Delhi</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Battuta was a fourteenth-century Moroccan traveller whose account of his journeys across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> is a major historical source. He served at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-bin-tughluq">Muhammad bin Tughluq</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> between 1334 and 1341, including as a judge. His observations are a valuable record of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta.jpg" alt="Ibn Battuta" width="291" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Léon Benett · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Handmade_oil_painting_reproduction_of_Ibn_Battuta_in_Egypt,_a_painting_by_Hippolyte_Leon_Benett..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
